From 49749fbfe200f20e18fad33dc0f3af02de2132c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:51:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: refuse creates onto a gate-only assignee
 (kanban.gate_only_assignees)

Five-whys t_01a1d08fbacf4432 (stranded t_01a1cdf7bbf44625): since 10-28, 9 cards were created on the
mini's bb board with assignee bb-repair-native (8 by bb-dev/default workers via kanban_create, 1 by the
resume requester copying its target's assignee). The dispatcher spawned the native worker at once, bb_gate
reclaimed it ("native worker lacks gate authorization") and recorded native_rejected, so each card sat
unadmitted until a manual STANDARD-RENEWAL review. Prose (bb-self-fix skill) and detection (bb_stranded)
were already shipped; this enforces it at the failure point.

- New hermes_cli/kanban_gate_only.py: kanban.gate_only_assignees maps a profile only an admission gate may
  assign to the queue a new card waits under ({bb-repair-native: bb-queue}). Read like queue_assignees
  (active profile config + board home config); malformed entries are skipped.
- validate_create_assignment (every create_task: kanban_create tool, `hermes kanban create`, kernel
  producers) raises GateOnlyAssigneeError (a ValueError) naming the queue assignee to use instead.
- The resume requester files a gate-only target's recovery card under its queue; goal recovery never
  picks a gate-only profile.
- assign_task (bb_gate_assignment.mutate's path) is unchanged; nothing changes without the config key.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_gate_only.py 9 pass; 5 of them fail on base (create_task, worker
kanban_create tool, CLI create, resume requester, goal recovery); gate reassignment and no-config controls
pass on both. 8/8 mutants of kanban_gate_only.py killed. 16 related files (223 tests) green.
